{
  "type": "team-preparation",
  "date": "2026-06-08",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "PREVIEW: France vs Senegal — Bid to Avoid 2002 Replay",
      "emoji": "⚽",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "match",
          "headline": "France Open World Cup Campaign Against Senegal at MetLife Stadium",
          "body": "<cite index=\"2-6\">France face Senegal on 16 June at MetLife Stadium in New York, with kick-off at 21:00 CET</cite>. <cite index=\"25-7\">Kylian Mbappé captains the side at his third finals, despite recent struggles with a thigh injury</cite>. <cite index=\"26-11\">The teams have only met once prior, when Senegal defeated defending champions France 1–0 in a major upset at the opening match of the 2002 FIFA World Cup</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France", "Senegal"],
            "venue": "MetLife Stadium, East Rutherford, New Jersey",
            "group": "Group I",
            "isPreview": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Opponent Analysis: Senegal's Structure & Key Threats",
      "emoji": "🇸🇳",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "Senegal Employ 4-3-3/4-2-3-1 Flexibility with Counter-Attack Focus",
          "body": "<cite index=\"27-1,27-2,27-3\">Senegal have good flexibility to play either as a 4-3-3 or a 4-2-3-1, with Sadio Mane, Iliman Ndiaye and Ismaila Sarr as attacking players in support of Nicolas Jackson</cite>. <cite index=\"37-1,37-2\">Coach Pape Thiaw favours a 4-3-3 that leans on a stingy defence and pace in transition, with Senegal sitting deep when necessary, winning the ball through Gueye, and breaking fast through Sarr, Jackson, and Mané</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["Senegal"]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "Sadio Mané Remains Tournament Talisman Despite Age",
          "body": "<cite index=\"30-6\">Veteran forward and captain Sadio Mane, 34, is set to play in his last World Cup – he said he will retire from international football after the tournament</cite>. <cite index=\"36-13,36-14\">Mané, 34 and now at Al Nassr, leads the line as the nation's record scorer with 55 international goals and finished as top scorer in qualifying with five goals</cite>. <cite index=\"37-27\">His pace has dipped, but his touch and big-game instinct remain world class</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["Senegal"]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "Defensive Strength Built on Experience; Creative Weakness in Midfield",
          "body": "<cite index=\"33-14,33-15\">Senegal possess a strong backline evidenced in their AFCON win, conceding just two goals en route to the title, though they may find things tougher at the World Cup facing top strikers</cite>. <cite index=\"40-19,40-20\">Despite possessing wingers with impressive speed and dribbling skills, and defensively oriented midfielders, Senegal lacks midfielders capable of making incisive passes, making it difficult to penetrate tight defences</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["Senegal"]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "France Defensive Setup: Exploit Senegal's Midfield Gaps",
      "emoji": "🛡️",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "Target Senegal's Limited Creative Output Through Centre",
          "body": "<cite index=\"27-8,27-9\">Pape Gueye and Idrissa Gueye will be the more defensive midfielders for Senegal</cite>. France should position their creative playmakers—Aurélien Tchouaméni, Eduardo Camavinga's replacement, or Adrien Rabiot—to exploit the space between Senegal's dual defensive midfielders and back four. <cite index=\"40-6,40-7,40-8\">Senegal's striking aspect is their incredibly smooth transition from high-pressure pressing to low-block defence, though thanks to their excellent physical fitness and high tactical discipline, players maintain cohesion regardless of attacking or defending phases</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France", "Senegal"]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "Anchor Defence with Saliba & Upamecano Against Quick Transitions",
          "body": "<cite index=\"17-24,17-25,17-26\">Arsenal's William Saliba is an absolute rock in the centre of France's defence, with PSG's Dayot Upamecano offering blistering pace alongside defensive solidity, and Barca's Jules Kounde at right back</cite>. Senegal will attempt rapid transitions through Mané and Jackson; France's centre-backs must be alert to secondary runs and cut off passing lanes to the wings.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France", "Senegal"]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Attacking Plan: Overwhelm via Width and Early Pressing",
      "emoji": "⚔️",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "Exploit Wing Space Against Senegal's Fullback Pairing",
          "body": "<cite index=\"25-9,25-10,25-11,25-12\">Ousmane Dembélé partners Mbappé in attack, fresh from back-to-back Champions League triumphs with PSG, having scored 35 goals as PSG lifted the European Cup for the first time in 2024-25 and became only the second French player this century to claim the Ballon d'Or</cite>. With Dembélé's blistering pace and precision crossing, France should attack down the flanks early to stretch Senegal's full-backs—particularly left-back, where <cite index=\"33-16\">Kalidou Koulibaly, at the grand old age of 34, is showing a few signs of slowing down</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France", "Senegal"]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "Press High in Opening 20 Minutes; Control Idrissa Gueye",
          "body": "<cite index=\"27-29,27-30,27-31,27-32,27-33\">Idrissa Gueye remains one of the best tacklers in world football—even at the age of 36—with 19 tackles at AFCON 2025, more than any other Senegal player, and only two players across the tournament made more tackles than Gueye</cite>. France should avoid giving Senegal possession in midfield; aggressive pressing from Mbappé and Dembélé in the first 20 minutes can disrupt Gueye's distribution and force errors.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France", "Senegal"]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Key Matchups: Confirmed Squad Focus",
      "emoji": "🔄",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "Mbappé vs. Senegal's Central Defence",
          "body": "<cite index=\"25-7\">Kylian Mbappé captains the side at his third finals, despite recent struggles with a thigh injury</cite>. <cite index=\"25-8\">The Real Madrid forward has 56 goals for France, second only to Olivier Giroud's 57</cite>. Mbappé's recovery from injury will be critical; his directness versus <cite index=\"36-11\">Kalidou Koulibaly, who anchors the defence with 103 caps</cite>, will be the decisive duel.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France", "Senegal"]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "Dembélé vs. Jackson + Mané Combination",
          "body": "<cite index=\"36-15\">Chelsea's Nicolas Jackson, Crystal Palace's Ismaïla Sarr and Everton's Iliman Ndiaye complete an attacking quartet rich in Premier League pedigree</cite>. Dembélé's press resistance and carrying ability must be paired with France's fullback support. Senegal will attempt to use Jackson's physicality and Mané's craft to break lines; France's wing-backs (Theo Hernández or Jules Koundé) must balance attacking support with defensive cover.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France", "Senegal"]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "Maignan vs. Mané Finishing",
          "body": "<cite index=\"17-27\">Mike Maignan in goal will give any defence confidence</cite>. Senegal will look to Mané for clinical finishing on transitions; Maignan's distribution from the back and shot-stopping will be essential to prevent quick counters from becoming goals.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France", "Senegal"]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "France Squad Status: Official Injuries & Confirmations",
      "emoji": "🏥",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "team",
          "headline": "Hugo Ekitiké Ruled Out by Season-Ending Achilles Injury",
          "body": "<cite index=\"25-14\">Liverpool's Hugo Ekitiké, ruled out by a season-ending Achilles injury in April, is a notable but expected absentee</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France"]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "team",
          "headline": "Mbappé Carrying Thigh Injury but Included in Final Squad",
          "body": "<cite index=\"25-7\">Kylian Mbappé captains the side at his third finals, despite recent struggles with a thigh injury</cite>. <cite index=\"17-10\">He has also had to contend with several injuries and niggles this season, missing quite a few games – which makes his goal-scoring exploits all the more impressive</cite>. This is a monitoring situation; fitness updates from official team sources are required before match day.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France"]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "team",
          "headline": "Camavinga Omitted; Deschamps Cites Inconsistent Season",
          "body": "<cite index=\"11-3,11-4,11-5\">Camavinga was part of the France squad that finished runner-up in the last World Cup but was left out by coach Didier Deschamps, who said: 'He had a difficult season for him where he played less. He also had injuries'</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France"]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "team",
          "headline": "Mateta Preferred Over Kolo Muani in Final Squad",
          "body": "<cite index=\"11-28\">Crystal Palace forward Jean-Philippe Mateta was preferred to Randal Kolo Muani in the 26-man list</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France"]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "team",
          "headline": "Full Squad Depth: Attack-Heavy Selection",
          "body": "<cite index=\"11-22\">Deschamps is gifted with an impressive attacking reservoir including Kylian Mbappé, Ballon d'Or winner Ousmane Dembélé, rising star Désiré Doué, Michael Olise, Rayan Cherki and Maghnes Akliouche</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France"]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Deschamps' Legacy Mission: Context & Motivation",
      "emoji": "👤",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "breaking",
          "headline": "Deschamps' Final Tournament After 14 Years; Seeking Second World Cup Title",
          "body": "<cite index=\"25-4,25-5\">Didier Deschamps signs off on his record-breaking reign at the FIFA World Cup this summer, his final tournament after 14 years in charge of France. The 57-year-old has guided France to back-to-back finals and now hunts a fitting farewell</cite>. <cite index=\"17-5\">He will be desperate to list a second title as manager as a riposte to his critics and to cement his legacy as a serial winner</cite>.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France"]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tactical Prediction: Expert Opinion",
      "emoji": "🔮",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "tactical",
          "headline": "OPINION — France Should Control Possession and Tempo; Expect Dominant Win",
          "body": "Based on confirmed squad data and tactical profiles: France's midfield control through Tchouaméni and Rabiot should dominate Senegal's defensive pairing. Mbappé's pace, if injury permits a full run, will exploit Koulibaly's slowing legs; Dembélé's Champions League form adds a clinical edge. Senegal's counter-threat through Mané and Jackson is genuine but sporadic—Maignan and Saliba should manage it. France's attacking depth (Dembélé, Olise, Akliouche, Doué as options) versus Senegal's aging core (Koulibaly 34, Mané 34, Gueye 36) favours Les Bleus. Expect France to control territory early, exploit the wings, and secure a comfortable group-stage opening. A 2–0 or 3–1 victory seems most probable, though Senegal's organisation and set-piece threat via Gueye's deliveries cannot be discounted.",
          "metadata": {
            "teams": ["France", "Senegal"]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
